# hf.co/unsloth/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-GGUF:UD-Q4_K_XL-ctx128k — the compliance
# reading seat's Ollama fallback (auto-compliance::reading, compliance-mapping).
#
# The seat is oMLX-served (unsloth--Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-UD-MLX-4bit, aliased in
# omlx-general / omlx-reasoning); this tag is what the seat falls back to when
# oMLX is unhealthy, so it must hold the seat's own 131072-token window. The
# registered GGUF tags stop at ctx96k, which would truncate the seat's
# dual-document payload (standard + operator set, 6k-86k tokens).
#
# Same weights as the ctx96k parent — 0 extra bytes; only num_ctx changes.
# Qwen3.6-35B-A3B is a hybrid linear-attention qwen3_5_moe: 10 of 40 layers
# keep a growing KV cache (kvh 2, head_dim 256), so KV at 131072 is ~1.3 GiB
# at Ollama's q8_0 cache type on top of ~22 GiB of UD-Q4_K_XL weights.
#
# Create with:
#   ollama create hf.co/unsloth/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-GGUF:UD-Q4_K_XL-ctx128k \
#     -f config/modelfiles/qwen3.6-35b-a3b-ud-q4_k_xl-ctx128k.Modelfile
FROM hf.co/unsloth/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-GGUF:UD-Q4_K_XL-ctx96k
PARAMETER num_ctx 131072